Chr2	Araport11	gene	6888540	6891409	.	-	.	ID=AT2G15820;Name=AT2G15820;Note=endonuclease;curator_summary=Encodes a protein that promotes splicing of type II introns. otp51 mutants fail to splice intron 2 of plastid ycf3 transcripts%2C a factor required for the assembly of Photosystem I. Therefore%2C homozygous otp51 mutants have profound photosynthetic defects and can only survive in sucrose-supplemented in vitro cultures under low light conditions. OTP51 may also be involved in splicing several other transcripts and precursor forms of the trnL%2C trnG%2C trnI%2C and trnA transcripts also accumulate in otp51 mutants. Although OTP51 shares some homology with DNA endonucleases%2C it lacks key catalytic residues suggesting that it does not participate in DNA cleavage.;symbol=OTP51;full_name=ORGANELLE TRANSCRIPT PROCESSING 51;computational_description=ORGANELLE TRANSCRIPT PROCESSING 51 (OTP51)%3B FUNCTIONS IN: endonuclease activity%3B INVOLVED IN: photosystem I assembly%2C nuclear mRNA cis splicing%2C via spliceosome%2C Group II intron splicing%3B LOCATED IN: chloroplast%3B EXPRESSED IN: 21 plant structures%3B EXPRESSED DURING: 13 growth stages%3B CONTAINS InterPro DOMAIN/s: Pentatricopeptide repeat (InterPro:IPR002885)%2C LAGLIDADG DNA endonuclease (InterPro:IPR004860)%3B BEST Arabidopsis thaliana protein match is: Pentatricopeptide repeat (PPR) superfamily protein (TAIR:AT5G61990.1)%3B Has 8373 Blast hits to 4744 proteins in 190 species: Archae - 0%3B Bacteria - 4%3B Metazoa - 37%3B Fungi - 65%3B Plants - 8172%3B Viruses - 0%3B Other Eukaryotes - 95 (source: NCBI BLink).;Dbxref=PMID:14576160,PMID:18557832,PMID:22188563,PMID:22353560,locus:2044541;locus_type=protein_coding
