Chr2	Araport11	gene	7516330	7519662	.	+	.	ID=AT2G17290;Name=AT2G17290;Note=Calcium-dependent protein kinase family protein;curator_summary=Encodes calcium dependent protein kinase 6 (CPK6)%2C a member of the Arabidopsis CDPK gene family.  CDPKs contain an intrinsic Ca2+-activation domain with four EF hand Ca2+-binding sites.  CDPKs protein kinases have been proposed to function in multiple plant signal transduction pathways downstream of [Ca2+]cyt elevations%2C thus transducing various physiological responses.  CPK6 is expressed in both guard cells and mesophyll cells.  Functions in guard cell ion channel regulation.   ABA and Ca(2+) activation of slow-type anion channels and%2C interestingly%2C ABA activation of plasma membrane Ca(2+)-permeable channels were impaired in independent alleles of single and double cpk3cpk6 mutant guard cells.  Furthermore%2C ABA- and Ca(2+)-induced stomatal closing were partially impaired in these cpk3cpk6 mutant alleles.  The protein kinase CPK6 is shown in biochemical assays to be directly activated by elevations in calcium concentrations in the physiological range (Laanements et al.%2C 2013 PlantPhys.%3B PMID: 23766366). These data correlate with the in vivo function of CPK6 in Ca2+ and ABA activation of S-type anion channels (Mori et al.%2C 2006 PLoS Biol.%3B  PMID: 17032064) and the ability of CPK6 to mediate ABA activation of SLAC1 (Brandt et al.%2C 2012 PNAS%3B PMID: 22689970).;symbol=CPK6;Alias=ATCDPK3,ARABIDOPSIS THALIANA CALMODULIN-DOMAIN PROTEIN KINASE 3,ATCPK6,ARABIDOPSIS THALIANA CALCIUM-DEPENDENT PROTEIN KINASE 6;full_name=calcium dependent protein kinase 6;computational_description=calcium dependent protein kinase 6 (CPK6)%3B FUNCTIONS IN: in 6 functions%3B INVOLVED IN: regulation of anion channel activity%2C protein amino acid phosphorylation%2C N-terminal protein myristoylation%2C abscisic acid mediated signaling pathway%2C regulation of stomatal movement%3B LOCATED IN: cytosol%2C plasma membrane%2C membrane%3B EXPRESSED IN: 26 plant structures%3B EXPRESSED DURING: 15 growth stages%3B CONTAINS InterPro DOMAIN/s: Protein kinase%2C ATP binding site (InterPro:IPR017441)%2C EF-Hand 1%2C calcium-binding site (InterPro:IPR018247)%2C Serine/threonine-protein kinase domain (InterPro:IPR002290)%2C EF-hand-like domain (InterPro:IPR011992)%2C Calcium-binding EF-hand (InterPro:IPR002048)%2C EF-hand (InterPro:IPR018248)%2C Serine/threonine-protein kinase-like domain (InterPro:IPR017442)%2C Protein kinase-like domain (InterPro:IPR011009)%2C Serine/threonine-protein kinase%2C active site (InterPro:IPR008271)%2C Protein kinase%2C catalytic domain (InterPro:IPR000719)%2C EF-HAND 2 (InterPro:IPR018249)%2C Calcium-dependent protein kinase (InterPro:IPR020642)%2C Calcium/calmodulin-dependent protein kinase-like (InterPro:IPR020636)%3B BEST Arabidopsis thaliana protein match is: calmodulin-domain protein kinase 5 (TAIR:AT4G35310.1)%3B Has 133264 Blast hits to 125497 proteins in 3863 species: Archae - 149%3B Bacteria - 13464%3B Metazoa - 49073%3B Fungi - 17503%3B Plants - 30048%3B Viruses - 473%3B Other Eukaryotes - 22554 (source: NCBI BLink).;Dbxref=PMID:12102506,PMID:12068094,PMID:12372144,PMID:12805596,PMID:12912986,PMID:14557048,PMID:17032064,PMID:18433157,PMID:18650403,PMID:18775970,PMID:19029837,PMID:20217124,PMID:20733066,PMID:20978156,PMID:21477822,PMID:21681023,PMID:23766366,PMID:23922271,PMID:24019427,PMID:25661797,locus:2827528;locus_type=protein_coding
