Chr2	Araport11	gene	7568018	7570912	.	+	.	ID=AT2G17430;Name=AT2G17430;Note=Seven transmembrane MLO family protein;curator_summary=A member of a large family of seven-transmembrane domain proteins specific to plants%2C homologs of the barley mildew resistance locus o (MLO) protein. Controls pollen tube reception in synergids. The Arabidopsis genome contains 15 genes encoding MLO proteins%2C with localization in plasma membrane. Phylogenetic analysis revealed four clades of closely-related AtMLO genes. ATMLO7 belongs to the clade III%2C with AtMLO5%2C AtMLO8%2C AtMLO9%2C and AtMLO10. The gene is expressed in vegetative organs (RT-PCR experiments)and in pollen grains%2C as shown by GUS activity patterns. The expression of several phylogenetically closely-related AtMLO genes showed similar or overlapping tissue specificity and analogous responsiveness to external stimuli%2C suggesting functional redundancy%2C co-function%2C or antagonistic function(s).;symbol=MLO7;Alias=ATMLO7,NTA,NORTIA;full_name=MILDEW RESISTANCE LOCUS O 7;computational_description=MILDEW RESISTANCE LOCUS O 7 (MLO7)%3B FUNCTIONS IN: calmodulin binding%3B INVOLVED IN: cell death%2C defense response%3B LOCATED IN: integral to membrane%2C plasma membrane%3B EXPRESSED IN: 10 plant structures%3B EXPRESSED DURING: seedling growth%2C petal differentiation and expansion stage%3B CONTAINS InterPro DOMAIN/s: Mlo-related protein (InterPro:IPR004326)%3B BEST Arabidopsis thaliana protein match is: Seven transmembrane MLO family protein (TAIR:AT5G65970.1)%3B Has 35333 Blast hits to 34131 proteins in 2444 species: Archae - 798%3B Bacteria - 22429%3B Metazoa - 974%3B Fungi - 991%3B Plants - 531%3B Viruses - 0%3B Other Eukaryotes - 9610 (source: NCBI BLink).;Dbxref=PMID:12569425,PMID:16525893,PMID:20226671,PMID:21071669,locus:2827607;locus_type=protein_coding
