Chr2	Araport11	gene	7590295	7594195	.	-	.	ID=AT2G17480;Name=AT2G17480;Note=Seven transmembrane MLO family protein;curator_summary=A member of a large family of seven-transmembrane domain proteins specific to plants%2C homologs of the barley mildew resistance locus o (MLO) protein. The Arabidopsis genome contains 15 genes encoding MLO proteins%2C with localization in plasma membrane. Phylogenetic analysis revealed four clades of closely-related AtMLO genes. ATMLO8 belongs to the clade III%2C with AtMLO5%2C AtMLO7%2C AtMLO9%2C and AtMLO10. The gene is expressed during seedling growth%2C in cotyledons and hypocotyl%2C and in fruit abscission zone%2C as shown by GUS activity patterns. The expression of several phylogenetically closely-related AtMLO genes showed similar or overlapping tissue specificity and analogous responsiveness to external stimuli%2C suggesting functional redundancy%2C co-function%2C or antagonistic function(s).;symbol=MLO8;Alias=ATMLO8,MILDEW RESISTANCE LOCUS O 8;full_name=MILDEW RESISTANCE LOCUS O 8;computational_description=MILDEW RESISTANCE LOCUS O 8 (MLO8)%3B FUNCTIONS IN: calmodulin binding%3B INVOLVED IN: cell death%2C defense response%3B LOCATED IN: plasma membrane%3B EXPRESSED IN: 25 plant structures%3B EXPRESSED DURING: 14 growth stages%3B CONTAINS InterPro DOMAIN/s: Mlo-related protein (InterPro:IPR004326)%3B BEST Arabidopsis thaliana protein match is: Seven transmembrane MLO family protein (TAIR:AT5G65970.1)%3B Has 544 Blast hits to 526 proteins in 58 species: Archae - 0%3B Bacteria - 0%3B Metazoa - 0%3B Fungi - 0%3B Plants - 539%3B Viruses - 0%3B Other Eukaryotes - 5 (source: NCBI BLink).;Dbxref=PMID:12169696,PMID:12569425,PMID:16146321,PMID:16525893,locus:2053888;locus_type=protein_coding
