Chr2	Araport11	gene	8089411	8091736	.	-	.	ID=AT2G18660;Name=AT2G18660;Note=plant natriuretic peptide A;curator_summary=Encodes PNP-A (Plant Natriuretic Peptide A). PNPs are a class of systemically mobile molecules distantly related to expansins%3B their biological role has remained elusive. PNP-A contains a signal peptide domain and is secreted into the extracellular space.  Co-expression analyses using microarray data suggest that PNP-A may function as a component of plant defence response and SAR in particular%2C and could be classified as a newly identified PR protein. It is stress responsive and can enhance its own expression.;symbol=PNP-A;Alias=AtPNP-A;full_name=plant natriuretic peptide A;computational_description=plant natriuretic peptide A (PNP-A)%3B LOCATED IN: extracellular region%2C cell wall%3B EXPRESSED IN: 19 plant structures%3B EXPRESSED DURING: 13 growth stages%3B CONTAINS InterPro DOMAIN/s: Barwin-related endoglucanase (InterPro:IPR009009)%2C Pollen allergen%2C N-terminal (InterPro:IPR014734)%2C Rare lipoprotein A (InterPro:IPR005132)%2C Expansin 45%2C endoglucanase-like (InterPro:IPR007112)%3B BEST Arabidopsis thaliana protein match is: Barwin-related endoglucanase (TAIR:AT4G30380.1)%3B Has 232 Blast hits to 231 proteins in 52 species: Archae - 0%3B Bacteria - 11%3B Metazoa - 0%3B Fungi - 6%3B Plants - 214%3B Viruses - 0%3B Other Eukaryotes - 1 (source: NCBI BLink).;Dbxref=PMID:15763661,PMID:15593128,PMID:15908439,PMID:16115070,PMID:16258012,PMID:16299171,PMID:16648215,PMID:16766691,PMID:16920880,PMID:17142480,PMID:17194769,PMID:17163880,PMID:17581762,PMID:18307990,PMID:18307823,PMID:18356294,PMID:18650403,PMID:21478192,PMID:21550130,PMID:23612149,PMID:24755512,PMID:25505478,locus:2053983;locus_type=protein_coding
