Chr2	Araport11	gene	8631959	8637300	.	-	.	ID=AT2G20000;Name=AT2G20000;Note=CDC27 family protein;curator_summary=Required for cell division and cell differentiation in meristems. Encodes a homolog of the CDC27 subunit of the anaphase-promoting complex (APC). Unlike other CDC27 homologs in Arabidopsis%2C its transcription is cell cycle regulated. Strong hbt mutants give rise to seedlings that lack an anatomically recognizable quiescent center and differentiated columella root cap cells%2C the cell types derived from the wild-type hypophysis. Furthermore%2C they have no mitotically active root meristem and lack a differentiated lateral root cap.;symbol=HBT;Alias=CDC27b;full_name=HOBBIT;computational_description=HOBBIT (HBT)%3B FUNCTIONS IN: binding%3B INVOLVED IN: in 10 processes%3B LOCATED IN: anaphase-promoting complex%2C nucleus%2C cell plate%2C spindle%3B EXPRESSED IN: 23 plant structures%3B EXPRESSED DURING: 14 growth stages%3B CONTAINS InterPro DOMAIN/s: Tetratricopeptide TPR-1 (InterPro:IPR001440)%2C Tetratricopeptide-like helical (InterPro:IPR011990)%2C Tetratricopeptide repeat-containing (InterPro:IPR013026)%2C Tetratricopeptide repeat (InterPro:IPR019734)%3B BEST Arabidopsis thaliana protein match is: Tetratricopeptide repeat (TPR)-like superfamily protein (TAIR:AT3G16320.1)%3B Has 19127 Blast hits to 10740 proteins in 1344 species: Archae - 1126%3B Bacteria - 9300%3B Metazoa - 1888%3B Fungi - 782%3B Plants - 572%3B Viruses - 0%3B Other Eukaryotes - 5459 (source: NCBI BLink).;Dbxref=PMID:9425146,PMID:12368267,PMID:16938844,PMID:17944809,PMID:20706207,PMID:22167058,locus:2061649;locus_type=protein_coding
