Chr2	Araport11	gene	9844134	9845385	.	+	.	ID=AT2G23130;Name=AT2G23130;Note=arabinogalactan protein 17;curator_summary=AGP17 is a lysine-rich arabinogalactan-protein (AGP) and part of a multi-gene family of glycoproteins with approx. 50 members. It falls into one subclass with AGP18 and AGP19%2C other lysine-rich AGPs. 84%25 of its proline residues are hydroxylated to hydroproline and its heavy glycosylation accounts for appr. 69%25 of the molecular weight. The main glycosyl residues are arabinose (30.1%25) and galactose (55.1%25). Glycosyl linkages are consistent with type II arabinogalactans. AGP17 is predicted to have a glycosylphosphatidylinositol (GPI)anchor and is localized to the plasma membrane and Hechtian strands. It is expressed in young/old leaves%2C shoots%2C suspension cultures and flowers.;symbol=AGP17;Alias=ATAGP17;full_name=arabinogalactan protein 17;computational_description=arabinogalactan protein 17 (AGP17)%3B BEST Arabidopsis thaliana protein match is: arabinogalactan protein  18 (TAIR:AT4G37450.1)%3B Has 67144 Blast hits to 32658 proteins in 1837 species: Archae - 189%3B Bacteria - 18272%3B Metazoa - 17078%3B Fungi - 7544%3B Plants - 7608%3B Viruses - 2133%3B Other Eukaryotes - 14320 (source: NCBI BLink).;Dbxref=PMID:12068095,PMID:12177459,PMID:12805588,PMID:15235117,PMID:15377758,PMID:15840645,PMID:16244449,PMID:16935991,PMID:17142483,PMID:17217456,PMID:17294240,PMID:18334669,PMID:18650403,PMID:21069430,PMID:21165646,PMID:21489093,PMID:21849816,locus:2045309;locus_type=protein_coding
