Chr2	Araport11	gene	10713807	10724106	.	+	.	ID=AT2G25170;Name=AT2G25170;Note=chromatin remodeling factor CHD3 (PICKLE);curator_summary=Encodes a SWI/SWF nuclear-localized chromatin remodeling factor of the CHD3 group. Involved in post-germination repression of embryonic development. Acts with GA to establish repression of embryonic genes upon germination. Protein preferentially accumulates in differentiating tissues. Loss of function alleles are associated with expression of embryonic traits in adult plants and derepression of embryonic genes such as PHEROS1.  Is an extragenic suppressor of slr2 (SSL2).  Mutations in PKL (SSL2) restores lateral root formation in the slr2 mutant slr-1.  It was proposed that PKL/SSL2-mediated chromatin remodeling negatively regulates auxin-mediated LR formation in Arabidopsis.;symbol=PKL;Alias=CHD3,CHR6,CKH2,CYTOKININ-HYPERSENSITIVE 2,EPP1,ENHANCED PHOTOMORPHOGENIC 1,GYM,GYMNOS,SSL2,SUPPRESSOR OF SLR 2;full_name=PICKLE;computational_description=PICKLE (PKL)%3B CONTAINS InterPro DOMAIN/s: Protein of unknown function DUF1087 (InterPro:IPR009463)%2C Zinc finger%2C RING-type (InterPro:IPR001841)%2C Zinc finger%2C PHD-type%2C conserved site (InterPro:IPR019786)%2C Zinc finger%2C PHD-type (InterPro:IPR001965)%2C Protein of unknown function DUF1086 (InterPro:IPR009462)%2C Chromo domain (InterPro:IPR000953)%2C SNF2-related (InterPro:IPR000330)%2C DEAD-like helicase%2C N-terminal (InterPro:IPR014001)%2C Chromo domain-like (InterPro:IPR016197)%2C DNA/RNA helicase%2C C-terminal (InterPro:IPR001650)%2C Zinc finger%2C FYVE/PHD-type (InterPro:IPR011011)%2C Helicase%2C superfamily 1/2%2C ATP-binding domain (InterPro:IPR014021)%2C Zinc finger%2C PHD-finger (InterPro:IPR019787)%3B BEST Arabidopsis thaliana protein match is: chromatin remodeling factor%2C putative (TAIR:AT4G31900.1)%3B Has 20234 Blast hits to 17178 proteins in 1958 species: Archae - 161%3B Bacteria - 5176%3B Metazoa - 5098%3B Fungi - 4334%3B Plants - 1876%3B Viruses - 134%3B Other Eukaryotes - 3455 (source: NCBI BLink).;Dbxref=PMID:10570159,PMID:10535738,PMID:15147899,PMID:16547115,PMID:17010112,PMID:18463617,PMID:19704491,PMID:19680533,PMID:21357580,PMID:21441433,PMID:21464619,PMID:22452853,PMID:23128324,PMID:23314848,PMID:23505340,PMID:23733056,PMID:25539918,PMID:25581843,locus:2040184;locus_type=protein_coding
