Chr2	Araport11	gene	11140809	11143360	.	+	.	ID=AT2G26170;Name=AT2G26170;Note=cytochrome P450%2C family 711%2C subfamily A%2C polypeptide 1;curator_summary=Encodes a protein with similarity to thromboxane-A synthase%2C member of the CYP711A cytochrome P450 family. MAX1 is a specific repressor of vegetative axillary buds generated by the axillary meristem. Expressed in vascular traces in the rosette stem and axillary buds throughout plant development. Mutants have increased axillary branches. Along with MAX3%2C4 thought to mediate control of shoot branching via synthesis of a signal molecule which is transported over long distance mediated by MAX2. cDNA supports the existence of the longer transcript predicted for this locus%2C no cDNA isolated for shorter transcript. MAX1 downregulates 11 genes involved in flavonoid pathway (CHS%2C CHI%2C F3H%2C F3'H%2C FLS%2C DFR%2C ANS%2C UFGT%2C RT%2C AAC and GST).;symbol=CYP711A1;Alias=MAX1,MORE AXILLARY BRANCHES 1;full_name=cytochrome P450%2C family 711%2C subfamily A%2C polypeptide 1;computational_description=cytochrome P450%2C family 711%2C subfamily A%2C polypeptide 1 (CYP711A1)%3B FUNCTIONS IN: electron carrier activity%2C monooxygenase activity%2C iron ion binding%2C oxygen binding%2C heme binding%3B INVOLVED IN: carotenoid biosynthetic process%2C positive regulation of flavonoid biosynthetic process%2C regulation of meristem structural organization%2C secondary shoot formation%2C auxin polar transport%3B LOCATED IN: endomembrane system%3B EXPRESSED IN: 23 plant structures%3B EXPRESSED DURING: 13 growth stages%3B CONTAINS InterPro DOMAIN/s: Cytochrome P450 (InterPro:IPR001128)%2C Cytochrome P450%2C E-class%2C group I (InterPro:IPR002401)%2C Cytochrome P450%2C conserved site (InterPro:IPR017972)%3B BEST Arabidopsis thaliana protein match is: cytochrome P450%2C family 71%2C subfamily B%2C polypeptide 35 (TAIR:AT3G26310.1)%3B Has 34245 Blast hits to 33955 proteins in 1742 species: Archae - 52%3B Bacteria - 5395%3B Metazoa - 11