Chr2	Araport11	gene	11196996	11201102	.	+	.	ID=AT2G26300;Name=AT2G26300;Note=G protein alpha subunit 1;curator_summary=Encodes an alpha subunit of a heterotrimeric GTP-binding protein. The active GTP-bound form of GPA1 binds to the GTG1 and GTG2 abscisic acid (ABA) receptors and appears to affect their GTPase and GTP-binding activity%2C and hence%2C ABA binding abilities. GPA1 is a positive regulator in ABA-mediated inhibition of stomatal opening. Plants with recessive mutant alleles have complex phenotypes including: reduced brassinolide response%2C reduced cell divisions%2C round leaves%2C short hypocotyls.  It is likely to be involved in the signaling events that trigger unfolded protein response-associated cell death. GPA1 is also involved in sugar signaling.;symbol=GP ALPHA 1;Alias=ATGPA1,ARABIDOPSIS THALIANA G PROTEIN ALPHA SUBUNIT 1,GPA1,G PROTEIN ALPHA SUBUNIT 1;full_name=G protein alpha subunit 1;computational_description=G protein alpha subunit 1 (GP ALPHA 1)%3B FUNCTIONS IN: in 6 functions%3B INVOLVED IN: in 16 processes%3B LOCATED IN: plasma membrane%2C endoplasmic reticulum membrane%2C heterotrimeric G-protein complex%3B EXPRESSED IN: 25 plant structures%3B EXPRESSED DURING: 13 growth stages%3B CONTAINS InterPro DOMAIN/s: Plant G-protein%2C alpha subunit (InterPro:IPR002976)%2C Guanine nucleotide binding protein (G-protein)%2C alpha subunit (InterPro:IPR001019)%2C G protein alpha subunit%2C helical insertion (InterPro:IPR011025)%3B BEST Arabidopsis thaliana protein match is: extra-large GTP-binding protein 3 (TAIR:AT1G31930.3)%3B Has 3745 Blast hits to 3647 proteins in 408 species: Archae - 0%3B Bacteria - 0%3B Metazoa - 2360%3B Fungi - 766%3B Plants - 268%3B Viruses - 0%3B Other Eukaryotes - 351 (source: NCBI BLink).;Dbxref=PMID:9539444,PMID:9175885,PMID:7767602,PMID:7766894,PMID:8312737,PMID:1748292,PMID:2111018,PMID:11121078,PMID:11696344,PMID:11408654,PMID:11408655,PMID:12068128,PMID:12175065,PMID:12566580,PMID:12692321,PMID:12789341,PMID:12837948,P