Chr2	Araport11	gene	12666935	12671055	.	+	.	ID=AT2G29630;Name=AT2G29630;Note=thiaminC;curator_summary=Encodes a protein involved in thiamine biosynthesis. The protein is an iron-sulfur cluster protein predicted to catalyze the conversion of 5-aminoimidazole ribonucleotide (AIR) to hydroxymethylpyrimidine phosphate (HMP-P). A severe reduction of THIC levels in plants decreases vitamin B1 (thiamin diphosphate (TPP)) levels and also leads to changes in the levels of numerous other metabolites since so many primary metabolic enzymes require a TPP co-factor. thiC mutants are chlorotic and arrest in their development at the cotyledon stage. A N-terminal targeting sequence directs the THIC protein to the chloroplast stroma. The THIC transcript is regulated by a TPP riboswitch in the 3' UTR. THIC transcripts are observed in seedlings 5 or more days after germination%2C and light promotes the expression of this gene.;symbol=THIC;Alias=PY,PYRIMIDINE REQUIRING;full_name=thiaminC;computational_description=thiaminC (THIC)%3B FUNCTIONS IN: iron-sulfur cluster binding%2C catalytic activity%2C ADP-ribose pyrophosphohydrolase activity%3B INVOLVED IN: response to vitamin B1%2C detection of bacterium%2C thiamin biosynthetic process%3B LOCATED IN: chloroplast%2C chloroplast stroma%2C plastid%3B EXPRESSED IN: 28 plant structures%3B EXPRESSED DURING: 13 growth stages%3B CONTAINS InterPro DOMAIN/s: Thiamine biosynthesis protein ThiC (InterPro:IPR002817)%3B Has 4416 Blast hits to 4411 proteins in 1719 species: Archae - 238%3B Bacteria - 3466%3B Metazoa - 3%3B Fungi - 0%3B Plants - 61%3B Viruses - 0%3B Other Eukaryotes - 648 (source: NCBI BLink).;Dbxref=PMID:5364924,PMID:14576160,PMID:15047901,PMID:16500996,PMID:17337630,PMID:18048325,PMID:18218973,PMID:18184068,PMID:18332905,PMID:18433503,PMID:17993623,PMID:18533652,PMID:19812694,PMID:20525008,PMID:22214485,PMID:23148892,PMID:23341335,PMID:24161603,PMID:25014715,locus:2060604;locus_type=protein_coding
