Chr2	Araport11	mRNA	12666979	12671055	.	+	.	ID=AT2G29630.2;Parent=AT2G29630;Name=AT2G29630.2;Note=thiaminC;curator_summary=Encodes a protein involved in thiamin biosynthesis. The protein is an iron-sulfur cluster protein predicted to catalyze the conversion of 5-aminoimidazole ribonucleotide (AIR) to hydroxymethylpyrimidine (HMP) or  hydroxymethylpyrimidine phosphate (HMP-P). A severe reduction of THIC levels in plants decreases vitamin B1 (thiamin diphosphate (TPP)) levels and also leads to changes in the levels of numerous other metabolites since so many primary metabolic enzymes require a TPP co-factor. thiC mutants are chlorotic and arrest in their development at the cotyledon stage. A N-terminal targeting sequence directs the THIC protein to the chloroplast stroma. A conserved TPP-binding site is located in the 3' UTR of the At2g29630.2 gene model%2C and is predicted to function as a riboswitch. The riboswitch controls the  formation of transcripts with alternative 3' UTR lengths%2C which affect mRNA accumulation and protein production. THIC transcripts are observed in seedlings 5 or more days after germination%2C and light promotes the expression of this gene.  Recessive mutant isolated by Redei. Leaves but not cotyledons white%2C lethal%3B restored to normal by thiamine or 2%2C5-dimethyl-4-aminopyrimidine.;conf_class=2;symbol=THIC;Alias=PY,PYRIMIDINE REQUIRING;full_name=thiaminC;computational_description=thiaminC (THIC)%3B FUNCTIONS IN: iron-sulfur cluster binding%2C catalytic activity%2C ADP-ribose pyrophosphohydrolase activity%3B INVOLVED IN: response to vitamin B1%2C detection of bacterium%2C thiamin biosynthetic process%3B LOCATED IN: chloroplast stroma%2C chloroplast%2C plastid%3B EXPRESSED IN: 28 plant structures%3B EXPRESSED DURING: 13 growth stages%3B CONTAINS InterPro DOMAIN/s: Thiamine biosynthesis protein ThiC (InterPro:IPR002817)%3B Has 4416 Blast hits to 4411 proteins in 1719 species: Archae - 238%3B Bacteria - 3466%3B Metazoa - 3%3B Fungi - 0%3B Plants - 61%3B Viruses - 0%3B Other Eukaryotes - 648 (source: NCBI BLink).;conf_rating=****;Dbxref=PMID:16675665,PMID:12756322,PMID:18332905,PMID:18431481,gene:1005714819,UniProt:O82392
