Chr2	Araport11	gene	12980428	12985277	.	-	.	ID=AT2G30470;Name=AT2G30470;Note=B3 domain-containing transcription repressor VAL1;curator_summary=HSI2 is a member of a novel family of B3 domain proteins with a sequence similar to the ERF-associated amphiphilic repression (EAR) motif. It functions as an active repressor of the Spo minimal promoter (derived from a gene for sweet potato sporamin A1) through the EAR motif. It contains a plant-specific B3 DNA-binding domain. The Arabidopsis genome contains 42 genes with B3 domains which could be classified into three families that are represented by ABI3%2C ARF1 and RAV1. HSI2 belongs to the ABI3 family. It is expressed at similar levels in all organs. Treatment with 6%25 sucrose showed a slight increase in transcript levels after 24 h. No changes were observed after treatment with 50%C2%B5M ABA. It is localized in the nucleus via a nuclear localization sequence located in the fourth conserved region of the C-terminal B3 domain.;symbol=HSI2;Alias=VAL1,VP1/ABI3-LIKE 1;full_name=high-level expression of sugar-inducible gene 2;computational_description=high-level expression of sugar-inducible gene 2 (HSI2)%3B CONTAINS InterPro DOMAIN/s: Transcriptional factor B3 (InterPro:IPR003340)%2C Zinc finger%2C CW-type (InterPro:IPR011124)%3B BEST Arabidopsis thaliana protein match is: HSI2-like 1 (TAIR:AT4G32010.1)%3B Has 1263 Blast hits to 1242 proteins in 97 species: Archae - 0%3B Bacteria - 5%3B Metazoa - 31%3B Fungi - 0%3B Plants - 1168%3B Viruses - 0%3B Other Eukaryotes - 59 (source: NCBI BLink).;Dbxref=PMID:11118137,PMID:12954765,PMID:14671022,PMID:15894743,PMID:16941220,PMID:17158584,PMID:22476218,PMID:23314941,PMID:23505340,PMID:24043445,PMID:24168327,PMID:25367506,locus:2064417;locus_type=protein_coding
