Chr2	Araport11	gene	13464294	13471867	.	+	.	ID=AT2G31660;Name=AT2G31660;Note=ARM repeat superfamily protein;curator_summary=SAD2 (super sensitive to ABA and drought 2) encodes an importin beta-domain family protein likely to be involved in nuclear transport in ABA signaling.  Subcellular localization of GFP-tagged SAD2 showed a predominantly nuclear localization%2C consistent with a role for SAD2 in nuclear transport.  Mutation of SAD2 in Arabidopsis alters abscisic acid sensitivity.  SAD2 was ubiquitously expressed at low levels in all tissues except flowers.  SAD2 expression was not induced by ABA or stress. Loss of function mutations in SAD2 exhibit increased tolerance for UV stress%2C  increased production of UV protective secondary metabolites and suppression of nuclear localization of MYB4 (a repressor of UV stress response genes). Regulates microRNA activity.;symbol=SAD2;Alias=EMA1,enhanced miRNA activity 1,URM9,UNARMED 9;full_name=SUPER SENSITIVE TO ABA AND DROUGHT2;computational_description=SUPER SENSITIVE TO ABA AND DROUGHT2 (SAD2)%3B FUNCTIONS IN: protein transporter activity%2C binding%3B INVOLVED IN: protein import into nucleus%2C docking%2C protein import into nucleus%3B LOCATED IN: nucleus%2C nuclear pore%2C cytoplasm%3B EXPRESSED IN: 24 plant structures%3B EXPRESSED DURING: 13 growth stages%3B CONTAINS InterPro DOMAIN/s: Importin-beta%2C N-terminal (InterPro:IPR001494)%2C Armadillo-like helical (InterPro:IPR011989)%2C Armadillo-type fold (InterPro:IPR016024)%2C Exportin/Importin%2C Cse1-like (InterPro:IPR013713)%3B BEST Arabidopsis thaliana protein match is: ARM repeat superfamily protein (TAIR:AT3G59020.1)%3B Has 3689 Blast hits to 2792 proteins in 293 species: Archae - 3%3B Bacteria - 183%3B Metazoa - 1271%3B Fungi - 834%3B Plants - 368%3B Viruses - 60%3B Other Eukaryotes - 970 (source: NCBI BLink).;Dbxref=PMID:12620976,PMID:14523572,PMID:16889648,PMID:18854047,PMID:18831797,PMID:19234066,PMID:18713401,PMID:19626137,PMID:21984696,locus:2065939;locu