Chr2	Araport11	gene	14244951	14248155	.	+	.	ID=AT2G33670;Name=AT2G33670;Note=Seven transmembrane MLO family protein;curator_summary=A member of a large family of seven-transmembrane domain proteins specific to plants%2C homologs of the barley mildew resistance locus o (MLO) protein. The Arabidopsis genome contains 15 genes encoding MLO proteins%2C with localization in plasma membrane. Phylogenetic analysis revealed four clades of closely-related AtMLO genes. ATMLO5 belongs to the clade III%2C with AtMLO7%2C AtMLO8%2C AtMLO9%2C and AtMLO10. The gene is expressed during seedling growth%2C in cotyledon vascular system%2C and in stigma%2C anther and pollen grains%3B it was not expressed in rosette leaves%2C as shown by GUS activity patterns. The expression of several phylogenetically closely-related AtMLO genes showed similar or overlapping tissue specificity and analogous responsiveness to external stimuli%2C suggesting functional redundancy%2C co-function%2C or antagonistic function(s).;symbol=MLO5;Alias=ATMLO5,MILDEW RESISTANCE LOCUS O 5;full_name=MILDEW RESISTANCE LOCUS O 5;computational_description=MILDEW RESISTANCE LOCUS O 5 (MLO5)%3B FUNCTIONS IN: calmodulin binding%3B INVOLVED IN: cell death%2C defense response%3B LOCATED IN: integral to membrane%2C plasma membrane%3B EXPRESSED IN: 11 plant structures%3B EXPRESSED DURING: L mature pollen stage%2C M germinated pollen stage%2C 4 anthesis%2C petal differentiation and expansion stage%3B CONTAINS InterPro DOMAIN/s: Mlo-related protein (InterPro:IPR004326)%3B BEST Arabidopsis thaliana protein match is: Seven transmembrane MLO family protein (TAIR:AT1G42560.1)%3B Has 551 Blast hits to 537 proteins in 60 species: Archae - 0%3B Bacteria - 0%3B Metazoa - 0%3B Fungi - 0%3B Plants - 544%3B Viruses - 0%3B Other Eukaryotes - 7 (source: NCBI BLink).;Dbxref=PMID:12569425,PMID:14500793,PMID:16525893,PMID:16607029,PMID:17064408,PMID:18775970,locus:2051073;locus_type=protein_coding
