Chr2	Araport11	gene	14325206	14328978	.	-	.	ID=AT2G33860;Name=AT2G33860;Note=Transcriptional factor B3 family protein / auxin-responsive factor AUX/IAA-like protein;curator_summary=ettin (ett) mutations have pleiotropic effects on Arabidopsis flower development%2C causing increases in perianth organ number%2C decreases in stamen number and anther formation%2C and apical-basal patterning defects in the gynoecium. The ETTIN gene encodes a protein with homology to DNA binding proteins which bind to auxin response elements. ETT transcript is expressed throughout stage 1 floral meristems and subsequently resolves to a complex pattern within petal%2C stamen and carpel primordia.  ETT probably functions to impart regional identity in floral meristems that affects perianth organ number spacing%2C stamen formation%2C and regional differentiation in stamens and the gynoecium. During stage 5%2C ETT expression appears in a ring at the top  of the floral meristem before morphological appearance of the gynoecium%2C consistent with the proposal that ETT is involved in prepatterning apical and basal boundaries in the gynoecium primordium.  It is a target of the ta-siRNA tasiR-ARF.;symbol=ETT;Alias=ARF3,AUXIN RESPONSE TRANSCRIPTION FACTOR 3;full_name=ETTIN;computational_description=ETTIN (ETT)%3B FUNCTIONS IN: DNA binding%2C sequence-specific DNA binding transcription factor activity%3B INVOLVED IN: response to auxin stimulus%2C vegetative phase change%2C regulation of transcription%2C DNA-dependent%2C abaxial cell fate specification%2C auxin metabolic process%3B LOCATED IN: nucleus%3B EXPRESSED IN: 24 plant structures%3B EXPRESSED DURING: 13 growth stages%3B CONTAINS InterPro DOMAIN/s: Transcriptional factor B3 (InterPro:IPR003340)%2C Auxin response factor (InterPro:IPR010525)%3B BEST Arabidopsis thaliana protein match is: auxin response factor 4 (TAIR:AT5G60450.1)%3B Has 1211 Blast hits to 1200 proteins in 55 species: Archae - 0%3B Bacteria - 0%3B Metazoa - 7%3B Fungi - 0%3B Plant