Chr2	Araport11	gene	16356041	16359943	.	-	.	ID=AT2G39200;Name=AT2G39200;Note=Seven transmembrane MLO family protein;curator_summary=A member of a large family of seven-transmembrane domain proteins specific to plants%2C homologs of the barley mildew resistance locus o (MLO) protein. The Arabidopsis genome contains 15 genes encoding MLO proteins%2C with localization in plasma membrane. Phylogenetic analysis revealed four clades of closely-related AtMLO genes. ATMLO6 belongs to the clade IV%2C with AtMLO2%2C AtMLO3 and AtMLO12. The gene is expressed during early seedling growth%2C in root tips and cotyledon vascular system%2C in floral organs (anthers and stigma)%2C and in fruit abscission zone%2C as shown by GUS activity patterns. The expression of several phylogenetically closely-related AtMLO genes showed similar or overlapping tissue specificity and analogous responsiveness to external stimuli%2C suggesting functional redundancy%2C co-function%2C or antagonistic function(s).;symbol=MLO12;Alias=ATMLO12,MILDEW RESISTANCE LOCUS O 12;full_name=MILDEW RESISTANCE LOCUS O 12;computational_description=MILDEW RESISTANCE LOCUS O 12 (MLO12)%3B FUNCTIONS IN: calmodulin binding%3B INVOLVED IN: defense response to fungus%2C incompatible interaction%2C response to cyclopentenone%2C leaf senescence%2C cell death%2C defense response%3B LOCATED IN: plasma membrane%3B EXPRESSED IN: 16 plant structures%3B EXPRESSED DURING: 7 growth stages%3B CONTAINS InterPro DOMAIN/s: Mlo-related protein (InterPro:IPR004326)%3B BEST Arabidopsis thaliana protein match is: Seven transmembrane MLO family protein (TAIR:AT1G11310.1)%3B Has 552 Blast hits to 537 proteins in 59 species: Archae - 0%3B Bacteria - 0%3B Metazoa - 0%3B Fungi - 2%3B Plants - 545%3B Viruses - 0%3B Other Eukaryotes - 5 (source: NCBI BLink).;Dbxref=PMID:12569425,PMID:12609040,PMID:15181213,PMID:15772289,PMID:15824099,PMID:16525893,PMID:16732289,PMID:17194768,PMID:17704230,PMID:18252252,PMID:18334669,PMID:18603616,PMID:20023151,PMID