Chr2	Araport11	mRNA	17811935	17816772	.	-	.	ID=AT2G42810.2;Parent=AT2G42810;Name=AT2G42810.2;Note=protein phosphatase 5.2;curator_summary=Encodes a phytochrome-specific type 5 serine/threonine protein phosphatase. It dephosphorylates active Pfr-phytochromes. Controls light signal flux by enhancing phytochrome stability and affinity for a signal transducer. The gene is alternately spliced. This variant is an integral membrane protein localized to the ER and nuclear envelope. Belongs to one of the 36 carboxylate clamp (CC)-tetratricopeptide repeat (TPR) proteins (Prasad 2010%2C Pubmed ID: 20856808) with potential to interact with Hsp90/Hsp70 as co-chaperones.  It also regulates tetrapyrrole biosynthesis through the accumulation of Mg-ProtoIX and acts as a negative regulator of photosynthesis associated nuclear gene expression during chloroplast biogenesis and development.;conf_class=2;symbol=PP5.2;Alias=AtPP5,Arabidopsis thaliana protein phosphatase 5,PAPP5,Phytochrome-Associated Protein Phosphatase 5,PP5,PROTEIN PHOSPHATASE 5;full_name=protein phosphatase 5.2;computational_description=protein phosphatase 5.2 (PP5.2)%3B FUNCTIONS IN: protein binding%2C phosphoprotein phosphatase activity%2C protein serine/threonine phosphatase activity%3B INVOLVED IN: response to cadmium ion%2C nucleocytoplasmic transport%2C red or far-red light signaling pathway%3B LOCATED IN: nuclear envelope%2C integral to endoplasmic reticulum membrane%2C nucleus%2C cytoplasm%3B EXPRESSED IN: 23 plant structures%3B EXPRESSED DURING: 13 growth stages%3B CONTAINS InterPro DOMAIN/s: Tetratricopeptide TPR-1 (InterPro:IPR001440)%2C Metallophosphoesterase (InterPro:IPR004843)%2C Protein phosphatase 5 (InterPro:IPR011236)%2C Tetratricopeptide-like helical (InterPro:IPR011990)%2C Serine/threonine phosphatase%2C PPP5 (InterPro:IPR013235)%2C Tetratricopeptide repeat-containing (InterPro:IPR013026)%2C Tetratricopeptide repeat (InterPro:IPR019734)%2C Serine/threonine-specific protein phosphatase/bis(5-nucleos