Chr2	Araport11	gene	18245357	18248459	.	-	.	ID=AT2G44110;Name=AT2G44110;Note=Seven transmembrane MLO family protein;curator_summary=A member of a large family of seven-transmembrane domain proteins specific to plants%2C homologs of the barley mildew resistance locus o (MLO) protein. The Arabidopsis genome contains 15 genes encoding MLO proteins%2C with localization in plasma membrane. Phylogenetic analysis revealed four clades of closely-related AtMLO genes. ATMLO15 belongs to the clade II%2C with ATMLO13 and ATMLO15. The gene is expressed during early seedling growth%2C in root tips and flower (papillae%2C anthers and pollen grains)%2C as shown by GUS activity patterns. The expression of several phylogenetically closely-related AtMLO genes showed similar or overlapping tissue specificity and analogous responsiveness to external stimuli%2C suggesting functional redundancy%2C co-function%2C or antagonistic function(s).;symbol=MLO15;Alias=ATMLO15,MILDEW RESISTANCE LOCUS O 15;full_name=MILDEW RESISTANCE LOCUS O 15;computational_description=MILDEW RESISTANCE LOCUS O 15 (MLO15)%3B FUNCTIONS IN: calmodulin binding%3B INVOLVED IN: cell death%2C defense response%3B LOCATED IN: integral to membrane%3B EXPRESSED IN: male gametophyte%2C root tip%2C root%2C papillae%3B CONTAINS InterPro DOMAIN/s: Mlo-related protein (InterPro:IPR004326)%3B BEST Arabidopsis thaliana protein match is: Seven transmembrane MLO family protein (TAIR:AT4G02600.2)%3B Has 552 Blast hits to 534 proteins in 57 species: Archae - 0%3B Bacteria - 0%3B Metazoa - 0%3B Fungi - 0%3B Plants - 548%3B Viruses - 0%3B Other Eukaryotes - 4 (source: NCBI BLink).;Dbxref=PMID:12569425,PMID:15047898,PMID:16525893,PMID:17064408,PMID:17408486,PMID:25506769,locus:2051859;locus_type=protein_coding
