Chr2	Araport11	gene	19033586	19036683	.	+	.	ID=AT2G46370;Name=AT2G46370;Note=Auxin-responsive GH3 family protein;curator_summary=Encodes a jasmonate-amido synthetase that is a member of the GH3 family of proteins. JAR1 catalyzes the formation of a biologically active jasmonyl-isoleucine (JA-Ile) conjugate. JA-Ile promotes the interaction between JAZ1 and COI1 in the jasmonate signaling pathway. JAR1 localizes to the cytoplasm and is also a phytochrome A signaling component. JAR1 is an auxin-induced gene. Loss of function mutants are defective in a variety of responses to jasmonic acid. JAR1 has additional enzymatic activities in vitro%2C (e.g. the ability to synthesize adenosine 5'-tetraphosphate and other JA conjugates)%2C but there are no data to show whether JAR1 catalyzes many of these reactions in vivo. JAR1 is involved in pathogen defense%2C sensitivity to ozone%2C and wound responses.;symbol=JAR1;Alias=AtGH3.11,FIN219,FAR-RED INSENSITIVE 219;full_name=JASMONATE RESISTANT 1;computational_description=JASMONATE RESISTANT 1 (JAR1)%3B FUNCTIONS IN: catalytic activity%2C adenylyltransferase activity%2C ATP binding%2C jasmonate-amino synthetase activity%3B INVOLVED IN: in 13 processes%3B LOCATED IN: vacuole%2C cytoplasm%3B EXPRESSED IN: 24 plant structures%3B EXPRESSED DURING: 13 growth stages%3B CONTAINS InterPro DOMAIN/s: GH3 auxin-responsive promoter (InterPro:IPR004993)%3B BEST Arabidopsis thaliana protein match is: Auxin-responsive GH3 family protein (TAIR:AT4G03400.1)%3B Has 1444 Blast hits to 1399 proteins in 231 species: Archae - 0%3B Bacteria - 474%3B Metazoa - 52%3B Fungi - 2%3B Plants - 663%3B Viruses - 0%3B Other Eukaryotes - 253 (source: NCBI BLink).;Dbxref=PMID:10921909,PMID:10886772,PMID:10036774,PMID:9807813,PMID:9724702,PMID:8758979,PMID:11041881,PMID:11041879,PMID:11090217,PMID:11607311,PMID:11449056,PMID:12084835,PMID:12059104,PMID:12172836,PMID:12236603,PMID:12445126,PMID:12376653,PMID:12509524,PMID:12694277,PMID:12744510,PMID:11722772,PMID:11006