Chr2	Araport11	mRNA	19033790	19036659	.	+	.	ID=AT2G46370.3;Parent=AT2G46370;Name=AT2G46370.3;Note=Auxin-responsive GH3 family protein;curator_summary=Encodes a jasmonate-amido synthetase that is a member of the GH3 family of proteins. JAR1 catalyzes the formation of a biologically active jasmonyl-isoleucine (JA-Ile) conjugate. JA-Ile promotes the interaction between JAZ1 and COI1 in the jasmonate signaling pathway. JAR1 localizes to the cytoplasm and is also a phytochrome A signaling component. JAR1 is an auxin-induced gene. Loss of function mutants are defective in a variety of responses to jasmonic acid. JAR1 has additional enzymatic activities in vitro%2C (e.g. the ability to synthesize adenosine 5'-tetraphosphate and other JA conjugates)%2C but there are no data to show whether JAR1 catalyzes many of these reactions in vivo. JAR1 is involved in pathogen defense%2C sensitivity to ozone%2C and wound responses.;conf_class=3;symbol=JAR1;Alias=AtGH3.11,FIN219,FAR-RED INSENSITIVE 219;full_name=JASMONATE RESISTANT 1;computational_description=JASMONATE RESISTANT 1 (JAR1)%3B FUNCTIONS IN: catalytic activity%2C adenylyltransferase activity%2C ATP binding%2C jasmonate-amino synthetase activity%3B INVOLVED IN: in 13 processes%3B LOCATED IN: cytoplasm%3B EXPRESSED IN: 24 plant structures%3B EXPRESSED DURING: 13 growth stages%3B CONTAINS InterPro DOMAIN/s: GH3 auxin-responsive promoter (InterPro:IPR004993)%3B BEST Arabidopsis thaliana protein match is: Auxin-responsive GH3 family protein (TAIR:AT4G03400.1)%3B Has 1356 Blast hits to 1352 proteins in 227 species: Archae - 0%3B Bacteria - 427%3B Metazoa - 52%3B Fungi - 2%3B Plants - 657%3B Viruses - 0%3B Other Eukaryotes - 218 (source: NCBI BLink).;conf_rating=****;Dbxref=PMID:16732289,gene:4010712452,UniProt:Q9SKE2-3
